      "updated": 1787146514655,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Instagram system design from software engineering Plus integrating AI/ML stuff\n\nInstagram isn’t just a photo-sharing app. It’s a hyper-scale social network, serving:\n\nOver 2 billion users monthly,\nHundreds of millions of posts daily,\nBillions of feed views, likes, comments, and stories each day.\n\n\n Functional Requirements\n    Users should be able to sign up, log in, and maintain profiles.\n    Users can upload photos & videos with captions.\n    Users can follow/unfollow other users.\n    Users should see a personalized feed of posts from accounts they follow, ranked by relevance.\n    Users can like, comment, and share posts.\n    Users can view ephemeral stories, disappearing after 24 hours.\n    Notifications for likes/comments/follows.\n\n Non-Functional Requirements\n    High availability: Instagram can’t afford downtime; target 99.99%.\n    Low latency: Feed loads in under 200ms globally.\n    Scalability: System should handle hundreds of millions of DAUs generating billions of reads and writes daily.\n    Eventual consistency: It’s acceptable for a slight delay in seeing new posts or likes.\n    Durability: No data loss on photos/videos.\n\nEstimations & Capacity Planning\n\n Daily Active Users (DAUs)\n    Assume 500 million DAUs.\n\n Posts\n    Average 1 photo/video post per user per day.\n    ➔ 500M posts/day.\n\n Feed Reads\n    Assume each user opens the app 10 times/day.\n\nEach time loads the feed.\n\n➔ 5 billion feed reads/day.\n\n💬 Likes & Comments\nEach user likes 20 posts/day and comments 2 times/day.\n\n➔ 10 billion likes/day, 1 billion comments/day.\n\n Storage\nAverage photo = 500 KB, video = 5 MB (average across formats).\nIf 70% are photos, 30% are short videos, blended avg ≈ 1.5 MB/post.\n\n➔ 500M posts/day × 1.5MB = 750 TB/day\n\nRetained indefinitely = petabytes scale storage.\n\n Throughput\nWrite-heavy ops:\nRead-heavy ops:\n\nPeak hour traffic typically 3x average, so we design for:\n\n~20,000 writes/sec for posts\n~350,000 writes/sec for likes/comments\n~175,000 feed reads/sec.\n\n Derived requirements\n    ResourceEstimated LoadPosts DB6K writes/sec, \n    PB-scale storageFeed service175K reads/secLikes/comments DB350K writes/sec,\n     heavy fan-outsMedia store~750 TB/day ingest, geo-cachedNotifications~100K events/sec on Kafka\n\n2. API Design\n\nInstagram APIs mainly support users, posts, feeds, interactions, stories, and notifications.\n\nAPI        Purpose\nPOST /signup                 Register a new user\n\nPOST /login        Authenticate user\n\nGET /users/{id}        Get user profile\n\nPOST /users/{id}/follow        Follow/unfollow user\n\nPOST /posts        Create photo/video post\n\nGET /posts/{id}        Get post details\n\nPOST /posts/{id}/like        Like/unlike post\n\nGET /posts/{id}/comments        Get comments\n\nGET /feed        Get personalized feed\n\nPOST /stories        Create story\n\nGET /stories        Get followed users' stories\n\nGET /notifications        Get user notifications\n\nKey design points:\n\nUse cursor-based pagination for feeds and comments.\n\nUse authentication tokens (OAuth/JWT/session tokens).\nApply rate limiting to write APIs.\nUse REST/GraphQL depending on client/query requirements.\nMedia should be uploaded to object storage + CDN, rather than passing large files through application servers.\n\n\n3. Database & Indexing\n\nInstagram needs high read/write scalability, especially for posts, likes, comments, and feeds.\n\nSharded MySQL/PostgreSQL → Users, posts, comments, relationships\nCassandra / Wide-column DB → Feed/timeline data and high-volume writes\nRedis → Hot data, caching, counters, sessions\nElasticsearch → User, hashtag, and content search\nObject Storage + CDN → Photos/videos\n\nKey design points:\n\nSharding → distribute data across multiple DB nodes.\nIndexes → optimize frequent queries such as user_id, post_id, created_at.\nReplication → provide high availability and read scalability.\nCaching → reduce database load and improve latency.\n\nWe use sharded relational storage for core entities, \nCassandra for high-scale feed data, Redis for caching, \nElasticsearch for search, and object storage/CDN for media.\n\n                         ┌─────────────────┐\n                         │  Mobile / Web   │\n                         │     Client      │\n                         └────────┬────────┘\n                                  │\n                                  ▼\n                         ┌─────────────────┐\n                         │   DNS / GeoDNS  │\n                         └────────┬────────┘\n                                  │\n                                  ▼\n                         ┌─────────────────┐\n                         │ Load Balancer   │\n                         └────────┬────────┘\n                                  │\n                                  ▼\n                         ┌─────────────────┐\n                         │   API Gateway   │\n                         └────────┬────────┘\n                                  │\n                    ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐\n                    ▼             ▼             ▼\n              ┌──────────┐ ┌──────────┐ ┌──────────────┐\n              │ Read     │ │ Write    │ │ Feed /       │\n              │ Service  │ │ Service  │ │ Ranking      │\n              └────┬─────┘ └────┬─────┘ └──────┬───────┘\n                   │            │               │\n                   ▼            ▼               ▼\n              ┌────────┐   ┌──────────┐   ┌──────────┐\n              │ Redis  │   │ Database │   │ ML Ranker│\n              │ Cache  │   │          │   └────┬─────┘\n              └────────┘   └────┬─────┘        │\n                                │               │\n                                ▼               ▼\n                           ┌────────────────────────┐\n                           │ Kafka / Event Queue     │\n                           └───────┬───────┬────────┘\n                                   │       │\n                         ┌─────────┘       └──────────┐\n                         ▼                            ▼\n                  ┌──────────────┐             ┌──────────────┐\n                  │ Feed Workers │             │ Notification │\n                  └──────┬───────┘             │   Workers    │\n                         │                     └──────────────┘\n                         ▼\n                  ┌──────────────┐\n                  │ Feed Store / │\n                  │ Feed Cache   │\n                  └──────────────┘\n\n\n        Media Upload / Delivery\n                 │\n                 ▼\n        ┌─────────────────┐\n        │ Object Storage  │\n        └────────┬────────┘\n                 │\n                 ▼\n        ┌─────────────────┐\n        │ Media Processing│\n        │ / Transcoding   │\n        └────────┬────────┘\n                 │\n                 ▼\n        ┌─────────────────┐\n        │      CDN        │\n        └────────┬────────┘\n                 │\n                 ▼\n             Client\n\nClient → DNS → Load Balancer\n\nDNS routes users to an appropriate region/edge, while the load balancer distributes traffic across healthy servers.\n\n API Gateway\n\nAuthentication, rate limiting, routing and request management.\n\n Application Services\n\nHandle user, post, comment, like, follow and feed operations.\n\n Database\n\nStores core metadata such as users, posts, comments and relationships. Data is sharded and replicated for scale and availability.\n\n Redis\n\nCaches frequently accessed data such as profiles, feed candidates, counters and sessions.\n\n Kafka / Event Queue\n\nDecouples asynchronous work such as feed generation, notifications, media processing and analytics.\n\n Feed Service\n\nGenerates feed candidates using followers/posts and sends them to the ranking system.\n\n ML Ranking\n\nRanks candidate posts based on user interests, engagement probability, freshness and other features.\n\n🖼️ Object Storage\n\nStores large media files such as photos and videos separately from metadata databases.\n\n Media Processing\n\nCreates optimized image/video versions, thumbnails and different resolutions asynchronously.\n\n CDN\n\nDelivers media from locations close to users, reducing latency and origin traffic.\n\nthis is high level design\n\n                         ┌──────────────┐\n                         │    Client    │\n                         │ iOS / Android│\n                         └──────┬───────┘\n                                │\n                                ▼\n                              DNS\n                                │\n                                ▼\n                         Load Balancer\n                                │\n                                ▼\n                       ┌─────────────────┐\n                       │   API Gateway   │\n                       └────────┬────────┘\n                                │\n                  ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐\n                  │                           │\n               READ                         WRITE\n                  │                           │\n                  ▼                           ▼\n           Read App Servers            Write App Servers\n                  │                           │\n        ┌─────────┼─────────┐         ┌───────┼─────────┐\n        │         │         │         │       │         │\n        ▼         ▼         ▼         ▼       ▼         ▼\n      Cache    Search     Feed      Blob    Queue    Metadata\n                 Index     Data    Storage\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    7. CLIENT EXPERIENCE                     │\n│                 Instagram App / Web                         │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    6. ML DECISION LAYER                     │\n│      Retrieval → Ranking → Re-ranking → Personalization     │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    5. INTELLIGENCE LAYER                    │\n│   CV / NLP / Embeddings / Moderation / LLM / Recommendations│\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    4. DATA + ML PLATFORM                    │\n│   Kafka → Data Lake → Feature Store → Training → Registry  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    3. APPLICATION SERVICES                  │\n│ Feed / Post / Comment / Follow / Search / Notification     │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    2. STORAGE + INFRASTRUCTURE              │\n│ DB / Cache / Object Storage / CDN / Search / Queues         │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    1. EDGE / NETWORK                        │\n│ DNS → CDN → Load Balancer → API Gateway                    │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n\n\n\nwe will discuss from layer 4 to layer 7 that is for data science and AI/Ml system design",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Instagram system design from software engineering Plus integrating AI/ML stuff\n\nInstagram isn’t just a photo-sharing app. It’s a hyper-scale social network, serving:\n\nOver 2 billion users monthly,\nHundreds of millions of posts daily,\nBillions of feed views, likes, comments, and stories each day.\n\n\n Functional Requirements\n    Users should be able to sign up, log in, and maintain profiles.\n    Users can upload photos & videos with captions.\n    Users can follow/unfollow other users.\n    Users should see a personalized feed of posts from accounts they follow, ranked by relevance.\n    Users can like, comment, and share posts.\n    Users can view ephemeral stories, disappearing after 24 hours.\n    Notifications for likes/comments/follows.\n\n Non-Functional Requirements\n    High availability: Instagram can’t afford downtime; target 99.99%.\n    Low latency: Feed loads in under 200ms globally.\n    Scalability: System should handle hundreds of millions of DAUs generating billions of reads and writes daily.\n    Eventual consistency: It’s acceptable for a slight delay in seeing new posts or likes.\n    Durability: No data loss on photos/videos.\n\nEstimations & Capacity Planning\n\n Daily Active Users (DAUs)\n    Assume 500 million DAUs.\n\n Posts\n    Average 1 photo/video post per user per day.\n    ➔ 500M posts/day.\n\n Feed Reads\n    Assume each user opens the app 10 times/day.\n\nEach time loads the feed.\n\n➔ 5 billion feed reads/day.\n\n💬 Likes & Comments\nEach user likes 20 posts/day and comments 2 times/day.\n\n➔ 10 billion likes/day, 1 billion comments/day.\n\n Storage\nAverage photo = 500 KB, video = 5 MB (average across formats).\nIf 70% are photos, 30% are short videos, blended avg ≈ 1.5 MB/post.\n\n➔ 500M posts/day × 1.5MB = 750 TB/day\n\nRetained indefinitely = petabytes scale storage.\n\n Throughput\nWrite-heavy ops:\nRead-heavy ops:\n\nPeak hour traffic typically 3x average, so we design for:\n\n~20,000 writes/sec for posts\n~350,000 writes/sec for likes/comments\n~175,000 feed reads/sec.\n\n Derived requirements\n    ResourceEstimated LoadPosts DB6K writes/sec, \n    PB-scale storageFeed service175K reads/secLikes/comments DB350K writes/sec,\n     heavy fan-outsMedia store~750 TB/day ingest, geo-cachedNotifications~100K events/sec on Kafka\n\n2. API Design\n\nInstagram APIs mainly support users, posts, feeds, interactions, stories, and notifications.\n\nAPI        Purpose\nPOST /signup                 Register a new user\n\nPOST /login        Authenticate user\n\nGET /users/{id}        Get user profile\n\nPOST /users/{id}/follow        Follow/unfollow user\n\nPOST /posts        Create photo/video post\n\nGET /posts/{id}        Get post details\n\nPOST /posts/{id}/like        Like/unlike post\n\nGET /posts/{id}/comments        Get comments\n\nGET /feed        Get personalized feed\n\nPOST /stories        Create story\n\nGET /stories        Get followed users' stories\n\nGET /notifications        Get user notifications\n\nKey design points:\n\nUse cursor-based pagination for feeds and comments.\n\nUse authentication tokens (OAuth/JWT/session tokens).\nApply rate limiting to write APIs.\nUse REST/GraphQL depending on client/query requirements.\nMedia should be uploaded to object storage + CDN, rather than passing large files through application servers.\n\n\n3. Database & Indexing\n\nInstagram needs high read/write scalability, especially for posts, likes, comments, and feeds.\n\nSharded MySQL/PostgreSQL → Users, posts, comments, relationships\nCassandra / Wide-column DB → Feed/timeline data and high-volume writes\nRedis → Hot data, caching, counters, sessions\nElasticsearch → User, hashtag, and content search\nObject Storage + CDN → Photos/videos\n\nKey design points:\n\nSharding → distribute data across multiple DB nodes.\nIndexes → optimize frequent queries such as user_id, post_id, created_at.\nReplication → provide high availability and read scalability.\nCaching → reduce database load and improve latency.\n\nWe use sharded relational storage for core entities, \nCassandra for high-scale feed data, Redis for caching, \nElasticsearch for search, and object storage/CDN for media.\n\n                         ┌─────────────────┐\n                         │  Mobile / Web   │\n                         │     Client      │\n                         └────────┬────────┘\n                                  │\n                                  ▼\n                         ┌─────────────────┐\n                         │   DNS / GeoDNS  │\n                         └────────┬────────┘\n                                  │\n                                  ▼\n                         ┌─────────────────┐\n                         │ Load Balancer   │\n                         └────────┬────────┘\n                                  │\n                                  ▼\n                         ┌─────────────────┐\n                         │   API Gateway   │\n                         └────────┬────────┘\n                                  │\n                    ┌─────────────┼─────────────┐\n                    ▼             ▼             ▼\n              ┌──────────┐ ┌──────────┐ ┌──────────────┐\n              │ Read     │ │ Write    │ │ Feed /       │\n              │ Service  │ │ Service  │ │ Ranking      │\n              └────┬─────┘ └────┬─────┘ └──────┬───────┘\n                   │            │               │\n                   ▼            ▼               ▼\n              ┌────────┐   ┌──────────┐   ┌──────────┐\n              │ Redis  │   │ Database │   │ ML Ranker│\n              │ Cache  │   │          │   └────┬─────┘\n              └────────┘   └────┬─────┘        │\n                                │               │\n                                ▼               ▼\n                           ┌────────────────────────┐\n                           │ Kafka / Event Queue     │\n                           └───────┬───────┬────────┘\n                                   │       │\n                         ┌─────────┘       └──────────┐\n                         ▼                            ▼\n                  ┌──────────────┐             ┌──────────────┐\n                  │ Feed Workers │             │ Notification │\n                  └──────┬───────┘             │   Workers    │\n                         │                     └──────────────┘\n                         ▼\n                  ┌──────────────┐\n                  │ Feed Store / │\n                  │ Feed Cache   │\n                  └──────────────┘\n\n\n        Media Upload / Delivery\n                 │\n                 ▼\n        ┌─────────────────┐\n        │ Object Storage  │\n        └────────┬────────┘\n                 │\n                 ▼\n        ┌─────────────────┐\n        │ Media Processing│\n        │ / Transcoding   │\n        └────────┬────────┘\n                 │\n                 ▼\n        ┌─────────────────┐\n        │      CDN        │\n        └────────┬────────┘\n                 │\n                 ▼\n             Client\n\nClient → DNS → Load Balancer\n\nDNS routes users to an appropriate region/edge, while the load balancer distributes traffic across healthy servers.\n\n API Gateway\n\nAuthentication, rate limiting, routing and request management.\n\n Application Services\n\nHandle user, post, comment, like, follow and feed operations.\n\n Database\n\nStores core metadata such as users, posts, comments and relationships. Data is sharded and replicated for scale and availability.\n\n Redis\n\nCaches frequently accessed data such as profiles, feed candidates, counters and sessions.\n\n Kafka / Event Queue\n\nDecouples asynchronous work such as feed generation, notifications, media processing and analytics.\n\n Feed Service\n\nGenerates feed candidates using followers/posts and sends them to the ranking system.\n\n ML Ranking\n\nRanks candidate posts based on user interests, engagement probability, freshness and other features.\n\n🖼️ Object Storage\n\nStores large media files such as photos and videos separately from metadata databases.\n\n Media Processing\n\nCreates optimized image/video versions, thumbnails and different resolutions asynchronously.\n\n CDN\n\nDelivers media from locations close to users, reducing latency and origin traffic.\n\nthis is high level design\n\n                         ┌──────────────┐\n                         │    Client    │\n                         │ iOS / Android│\n                         └──────┬───────┘\n                                │\n                                ▼\n                              DNS\n                                │\n                                ▼\n                         Load Balancer\n                                │\n                                ▼\n                       ┌─────────────────┐\n                       │   API Gateway   │\n                       └────────┬────────┘\n                                │\n                  ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐\n                  │                           │\n               READ                         WRITE\n                  │                           │\n                  ▼                           ▼\n           Read App Servers            Write App Servers\n                  │                           │\n        ┌─────────┼─────────┐         ┌───────┼─────────┐\n        │         │         │         │       │         │\n        ▼         ▼         ▼         ▼       ▼         ▼\n      Cache    Search     Feed      Blob    Queue    Metadata\n                 Index     Data    Storage\n\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    7. CLIENT EXPERIENCE                     │\n│                 Instagram App / Web                         │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    6. ML DECISION LAYER                     │\n│      Retrieval → Ranking → Re-ranking → Personalization     │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    5. INTELLIGENCE LAYER                    │\n│   CV / NLP / Embeddings / Moderation / LLM / Recommendations│\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    4. DATA + ML PLATFORM                    │\n│   Kafka → Data Lake → Feature Store → Training → Registry  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    3. APPLICATION SERVICES                  │\n│ Feed / Post / Comment / Follow / Search / Notification     │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    2. STORAGE + INFRASTRUCTURE              │\n│ DB / Cache / Object Storage / CDN / Search / Queues         │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                    1. EDGE / NETWORK                        │\n│ DNS → CDN → Load Balancer → API Gateway                    │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n\n\n\nwe will discuss from layer 4 to layer 7 that is for data science and AI/Ml system design",
